A ball is kicked from the ground and its height $h$ metres after $t$ seconds is shown.
What does the point where the curve meets the horizontal axis at $t=6$ tell you?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[width=7.5cm,height=7cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=-0.5,xmax=7,ymin=-1.2,ymax=10.5,xtick={0,1,...,6},ytick={0,1,...,10},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\scriptsize,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={$t$},ylabel={$h$}]
\addplot[thick,blue!70!black,domain=0:6,samples=100] {-x*x+6*x};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

